<article class="env-lemma" id="0GIM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GIM">Lemma <span data-tag="0GIM">10.154.4</span>.</a> Let $I$ be a directed set. Let $i \mapsto (R_ i \to A_ i)$ be a system of arrows of rings over $I$. Set $R = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits R_ i$ and $A = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_ i$. If each $A_ i$ is a filtered colimit of étale $R_ i$-algebras, then $A$ is a filtered colimit of étale $R$-algebras. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $A = A \otimes _ R R = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_ i \otimes _{R_ i} R$ and hence we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0BSJ" data-tag="0BSJ">10.154.3</a> because $R \to A_ i \otimes _{R_ i} R$ is a filtered colimit of étale ring maps by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BSH" data-tag="0BSH">10.154.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>